      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dutch Flat was founded by German brothers Joseph and Charles Dornbach in 1851 during the Gold Rush.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_Flat%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Mule drivers called the camp \"Dutch Charlie's Flat,\" giving the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_Flat%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1853, Dutch Flat boasted one of California's largest Chinese settlements, with 3,500 of its 6,000 residents being Chinese.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://beyond.nvexpeditions.com/california/placer/dutchflat.php",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town lost its stagecoach prominence after the railroad reached Cisco in 1866, ending its role as a major stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://beyond.nvexpeditions.com/california/placer/dutchflat.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dutch Flat is a California Historical Landmark, and residents are pushing for a state sign on I‑80 to highlight this status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_Flat%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Golden Drift Historical Society preserves Dutch Flat’s heritage through museum tours and community events.",
